# Every SVG in this directory, with the SHA-256 of the bytes that were
# COMPARED BYTE FOR BYTE against src/icons/<same name>.svg on
# microsoft/vscode-codicons main, on 2026-09-09. Every file matched. The
# recipe is in the LICENSE beside this file, and it was run rather than
# quoted.
#
# THIS FILE IS WHAT STOPS THAT DATE OUTLIVING ITS EVIDENCE, which is the
# defect issue #442 records: the LICENSE carried a dated one-time check
# three paragraphs above its own argument that one-time checks are what
# rot. A date attached to a DIRECTORY silently covers whatever is added
# to it afterwards — and something already had been. book.svg arrived in
# d712a28c, the same commit that wrote "VERIFIED 2026-08-30", so the
# claim was stamped two days before the file it covered existed. The
# prose was consistent about book.svg being re-fetched; nothing
# connected the sentence to the bytes.
#
# So the verification is recorded against BYTES.
# TestTheVerifiedIconsAreStillTheVerifiedBytes fails the moment the
# directory and this file stop agreeing, in EITHER direction: an added
# icon is not covered, a changed icon is not the one that was compared,
# and a removed icon leaves a line describing nothing.
#
# When that test goes red, run the LICENSE's diff for the file it names
# and then update the line here. Editing this file to make the test pass
# without running the diff converts a checked claim back into an
# asserted one, which is the whole thing being fixed.
#
# No count is written here, deliberately — see the LICENSE.

